# Structural Enhancement & Activity Logging Plan for Factory-Flow

Comprehensive overhaul of Product pricing, Order creation & status management, Customer soft deletion, and an industry-standard Audit & Activity Logging module.

---

## Architecture & Data Flow Overview

```
 ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │                                   USER ACTION                                     │
 │  (Create/Update Customer, Product, Order, Status Change, Payment, Invoice)         │
 └─────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                           │
                                           ▼
 ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │                               BACKEND INTERCEPTOR                                 │
 │  1. Executes Domain Business Logic (Scoped by businessId)                         │
 │  2. Enforces Decimal Rounding (Math.round(val * 100) / 100)                        │
 │  3. Emits Audit Log Entry -> ActivityLog (userId, userName, action, details)      │
 └─────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                           │
         ┌─────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┐
         ▼                                 ▼                                 ▼
┌─────────────────┐               ┌─────────────────┐               ┌─────────────────┐
│     PRODUCT     │               │      ORDER      │               │   ACTIVITY LOG  │
│ - price         │               │ - status        │               │ - userId        │
│ - discountedPrc │               │ - paymentStatus │               │ - userName      │
│ - stock         │               │ - discount &    │               │ - action        │
└─────────────────┘               │   addlCharges   │               │ - entity & id   │
                                  │ - invoice PDF   │               └─────────────────┘
                                  └─────────────────┘
```

---

## Key Design Principles & Constraints

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Code-Level Enums Only**: All status and role enumerations (`OrderStatus`, `PaymentStatus`, `PaymentMethod`, `PriceType`, `Role`, `SubscriptionStatus`, `ActivityAction`) will be stored as `String` columns at the Database level, and strictly enforced via TypeScript types and DTO validators in code.

> [!NOTE]
> **2-Decimal Rounding**: All price calculations (unit price, subtotal, discount amounts, additional charges, and grand total) will be rounded off to 2 decimal places using a central utility (`Math.round(value * 100) / 100`).

